      "writtenOn": "2024-02-22T09:36:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think it is a good idea. An additional config like `HW_TEST_ON` would need to be introduced anyway to include CMake from zephyr/test/hwtest/. The complexity is mainly caused by RO/RW.\n\nAdditionally, the current version simplifies setting configs per test. Every test has to set `HW_TEST`, `HW_TEST_RW_ONLY` is set by default and if any test has to be run in RO, `HW_TEST_RW_ONLY` can be unset manually or even by test runner e.g. I use it [here](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/5310657/3/test/run_device_tests.py#791). I feel like using one choice for enabling and selecting RO/RW can introduce setting mutually exclusive configs.",
      "parentUuid": "668ecc96_814e6756",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "48218338c90f91a419c4fdf48e681e1d49f8ec46",
